## 1.1: IQHE
- Von Klitzing discovers plateaus in Hall resistance as a function of B-field (1980), quantized at
$\displaystyle R_H = \frac{h}{ne^2}$
    - note that n is an integer, not \$ of electrons
- quantization is a notable property of a macroscopic system independent of material, geometry, or sample
- “concurrent with the plateaus is a ‘superflow — dissipationless current flow as $T \rightarrow 0$
